(xy)^3 =x^3 y^3 The\space power\space of\space a\space product\space is\space the\space product\space of\space the\space powers.
MISTAKES
x^3 \cdot x^5 \not= x^{15} We\space should\space add\space the\space exponents.
(2x)^3 \not= 2x^3 2\space is\space also\space cubed.
(x +2)^3 \not= x^3 +8The\space product\space rule\space does\space not\space apply\space to\space sums.
2 \cdot 5^3 \not= 10^3 We\space compute\space powers\space before\space products.
